  "claims": [
    "A per-box deterministic simulation of one threaded state lifts constructively to every circuit of the original mixed syntax, including tensor and all copy/discard wires, without duplicating implicit state.",
    "Old/new actual native MAC prefixes followed by arbitrary nonempty MAC analysis circuits retain their full joint frame/output correspondence under final PC relocation.",
    "A supplied comparison cell in any higher basis of the actual unified MAC rules can be repaired at its exact internal footprint and connected to the old-to-optimized native-prefix correspondence.",
    "Both generic simulation and concrete native repair preserve arbitrary correlated past, old initial state and original data/transcript.",
    "The selected physical programs equal the outputs of the previously certified original/optimizing compilers.",
    "The physical prefix retains its respective stopping, request encoding, transcript encoding and four-call contracts; mixed analysis leaves its complete native-frame marginal intact.",
    "For the actual fixed-key-space MAC game, both implementations followed by arbitrary mixed analysis retain the complete original physical game law and inherited success upper bound 1/256.",
    "A concrete nonempty tensor/copy/discard analysis copies sampled full outcomes and retains state/trace, while a generated finite local association/crypto comparison is instantiated under such a context and passed to native repair."
  ],
