  "limits": [
    "The mixed MAC boxes are the original conditional analysis kernels, not newly compiled native instructions. 343/286 are physical caller-prefix bounds only, excluding analysis generation/execution/checking.",
    "The model uses one actual caller invocation followed by analysis of sampled output. It is not arbitrary interleaving of new effectful native programs or a compiler from the full mixed proof language.",
    "The general simulation theorem requires explicit per-box kernel contracts. Native execution evidence is not inferred from stochastic equality.",
    "Repair interprets both compared diagrams in the updated analysis model; arbitrary changes of model interpretations are not equated by transporting condition proofs.",
    "Physical game success bounds do not certify arbitrary extra adversary observations of analysis data, arbitrary attackers, or asymptotic security.",
    "Copying the oracle state snapshot inside a full outcome does not fork the running oracle state. Tensor threads one physical frame in its fixed order.",
    "A higher comparison cell is explicitly supplied or constructed by the partial local basis. Global finite-basis completeness, old-library higher projection and all remaining overlaps stay open.",
    "No equality of old/new clock processes at every horizon or pointwise speed dominance; an old false branch takes 285 while the new one takes 286.",
    "Native oracle internals and key generation remain externally accounted for. Mixed computational reduction extraction, contextual loss/resource contracts and total execution costs remain open.",
    "Counts exclude diagram/wire/boundary/code/library payload and dependency search. No compression or speed advantage over an equally informed ordinary shared proof is established."
  ],
